## 1. GenericOperationSource.cs
The generic parameter `T` on class `GenericOperationSource<T>` is used with `ModelReaderWriter.Read(response.Content, typeof(T))` and `Activator.CreateInstance(typeof(T), ...)`, both of which need `[DynamicallyAccessedMembers]`.

Add annotation to the class's type parameter `T`:
```csharp
internal class GenericOperationSource<[DynamicallyAccessedMembers(DynamicallyAccessedMemberTypes.PublicConstructors | DynamicallyAccessedMemberTypes.NonPublicConstructors)] T> : IOperationSource<T>
```

## 2. ArmOperation.cs
The generic methods `Rehydrate<T>`, `RehydrateAsync<T>`, and `IsResource<T>` use `typeof(T)` with `GetConstructor()` and `Activator.CreateInstance()`. Add `[DynamicallyAccessedMembers]` to the type parameter `T` on ALL THREE methods.

For `IsResource<T>()`:
```csharp
private static bool IsResource<[DynamicallyAccessedMembers(DynamicallyAccessedMemberTypes.PublicConstructors | DynamicallyAccessedMemberTypes.NonPublicConstructors)] T>() where T : notnull
```

For `Rehydrate<T>` and `RehydrateAsync<T>`, they call `IsResource<T>()` and `new GenericOperationSource<T>()`, so they need the same annotation:
```csharp
public static ArmOperation<T> Rehydrate<[DynamicallyAccessedMembers(DynamicallyAccessedMemberTypes.PublicConstructors | DynamicallyAccessedMemberTypes.NonPublicConstructors)] T>(...)
public static async Task<ArmOperation<T>> RehydrateAsync<[DynamicallyAccessedMembers(DynamicallyAccessedMemberTypes.PublicConstructors | DynamicallyAccessedMemberTypes.NonPublicConstructors)] T>(...)
```

Make sure to add `using System.Diagnostics.CodeAnalysis;` if not already present.

## 3. ArmClientBuilderExtensions.cs
The method `AddArmClient<TBuilder, TConfiguration>` calls `RegisterClientFactory<ArmClient, ArmClientOptions>(configuration)` which has `[RequiresUnreferencedCode]` and `[RequiresDynamicCode]`. Propagate these attributes to the calling method.

